{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/973659-random-funny-stories-from-your-campaigns","id":973659,"title":"Random funny stories from your campaigns?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-20T22:01:45-07:00","id":973659,"title":"Random funny stories from your campaigns?","content":"Just a random thread for random funny things that happened in your campaigns that are good enough to share.<br /> <br /> In one of my stories I served as an ST for (it was basically a VtM/VtR mashup), I was half-arsing making a Gangrel char to serve as an ally to the PC in the game. For some random reason I decided his backstory would include a part like this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Sometime during the Gangrel's life, he was in dog form due to Protean and in some night time dog contest. Randomness happened and he somehow was thought to be some contestant's dog, and someone looking to get the prize claimed him as his own. The Gangrel couldn't turn back due to the masquerade, so he went along with it and almost naturally won first prize. For some reason, the &quot;owner&quot; named him as &quot;Sparkles&quot; on local television. Funnily enough, more than a few vampires caught wind and could recognize who the dog actually was, leading to him becoming &quot;the dog show winner Sparkles&quot; by most vampires and the name won't likely wash off anytime soon.<br /> <br /> Later that week he murdered the guy who called him that. The end!&quot; <br /> <br /> Flash forwards about 50+ sessions where the PC and a bunch of other people (including Sparkles) are in the Underworld. Lo and behold, the murdered &quot;pet owner&quot; was down there and pissed off about being killed, cue him asking &quot;was it because I called you sparkles&quot; did it take for the other Vampire NPCs to uproar in laughter and for Sparkles to kill the &quot;pet owner&quot; a second time. As much as you can kill a ghost anyways. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:48:04-07:00","id":973953,"title":"","content":"Three words, sans-context because it's about four sessions away in the AP:<br /> <br /> <i>That fucking cat.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:32:43-07:00","id":973972,"title":"","content":"The fact that Santa Claus, as in the jolly fat present giving lovable father of Christmas, was almost responsible for accidentally destroying western civilisation.<br /> <br /> There was the time when were a bit stumped trying to track down the antagonist in a Changeling game so I used diviners madness to ask where they would be this evening. We got an answer, started making plans for an ambush then quoth my charachter &quot;Oh crap! I feel normal!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Turns out I got the multiple personalities Derangement with the other personality believing they were a normal human who sees the Freehold as a weird Cult that she's part of. The personalities switched after a battle ended resulting in her fleeing in a panic down a public street unaware that Armour of the Element's Fury was active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T17:08:20-07:00","id":974121,"title":"","content":"The Gun Fight That Never Happened.<br /> <br /> Two Acanthus come into a room. The <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>first </b></span>pisses the <b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">second </span></b>off, so the <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>second </b></span>shoots the <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>first</b></span>. But, the <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>first </b></span>has a triggered spell that causes time to go back a turn, and uses that interruption to draw his own gun and shoot the <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>second</b></span>. Except, the <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>second </b></span>has <i>exactly </i>the same triggered spell, and turns back time on the <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>first</b></span>.<br /> <br /> Back exactly where they started, they decided not to push the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T07:59:36-07:00","id":974416,"title":"","content":"Changelings game. We wanted to fight someone in a dream. We went in a pervert's one by accident...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/LQQeHD6.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So yeah we all wore corset &amp; tutu during the boss fight.... including the boss","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T08:17:54-07:00","id":974423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/973659-random-funny-stories-from-your-campaigns?p=974121#post974121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gun Fight That Never Happened.<br /> <br /> Two Acanthus come into a room. The <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>first </b></span>pisses the <b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">second </span></b>off, so the <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>second </b></span>shoots the <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>first</b></span>. But, the <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>first </b></span>has a triggered spell that causes time to go back a turn, and uses that interruption to draw his own gun and shoot the <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>second</b></span>. Except, the <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>second </b></span>has <i>exactly </i>the same triggered spell, and turns back time on the <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>first</b></span>.<br /> <br /> Back exactly where they started, they decided not to push the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that is pretty much the standard for when two Time mages <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=buE_jLEZrf4\" target=\"_blank\">fight</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:13:53-07:00","id":974546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/973659-random-funny-stories-from-your-campaigns?p=974423#post974423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that is pretty much the standard for when two Time mages <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=buE_jLEZrf4&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">fight</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't fight it; you already didn't win.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T10:14:58-07:00","id":975109,"title":"","content":"A Zeka (A nuclear Promethean) decided to live in a soccer stadium. Then Rio de Janeiro became a nuclear wasteland. It was a coincedence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11165-tangledvirus","name":"TangledVirus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T13:17:00-07:00","id":975196,"title":"","content":"In a Geist game I'm GMing for, a Sin Eater has recently arisen and is chasing her killer (another Sin Eater) down a mountainside. Unfortunately, she is hit with Phantasmal Curse 3, meaning all movements involving dexterity are reduced to a Chance Die. I had her roll to see if she could stop on the path. She rolled a 1. Cue newly arisen Sin Eater slipping and accidentally flinging herself down the side of the mountain. (Since this was in the first session I went easy on her and made it a not-bad landing via a slope and sod, at the cost of her losing her assailant).<br /> <br /> The really funny part is how she had her character go through a list of expletives as she fell. It was so hilarious I gave her a beat for it on top of the one she got for the dramatic failure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T18:31:27-07:00","id":976860,"title":"","content":"A vampire, a demon, and a sin-eater get waylaid by gangsters sorta-not-really-randomly. The vampire proceeds to beat the ever-living hell out of them, to the point of almost flipping the car the ones still standing were using to escape, making liberal use of his Celerity and his fists along the way.<br /> After finally letting them go, I then reminded the character that he was still wearing the maid uniform he, for some inexplicable reason, told me he decided to wear to clean a ghost's house<br /> .<br /> The group would then constantly relay the story about the insanely tough, maid-uniform-clad brawler that, one time, pretty much single-handily beat up 7 thugs in a minute, and almost flipped their car.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cThe good sleep better, but the bad seem to enjoy the waking hours much more.\u201d</b> -<i>Woody Allen</i> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":5322,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5322-zimthehacker","user":"Zimthehacker","date":". 09-26-2016, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5322-zimthehacker","name":"Zimthehacker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5322_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:34:02-07:00","id":978584,"title":"","content":"So, I was playing a Changeling game where we had just transitioned from the Hedge into our Beast player's lair, due to him having created a chamber in the Hedge he could use. Since the Hedge was still permuting the lair in a small way, and my Changeling was having a bad day with his rolls (very low Willpower and Glamour), I decided he'd want a place to lie down, and so he went to some dangling vines and tried to make them into a hammock. I failed the crafts roll, and opted to make it a dramatic failure.<br /> <br /> Cue the vines wrapping around my Changeling instead, and me singing an impromptu version of &quot;Do You Want to Build a Snowman&quot; that went something like this:<br /> <br /> <i>Do you want to build a hammock?<br /> Come on let's get these vines right down.<br /> Here they grab at you, holding you,<br /> You're the hammock now~</i><br /> <br /> Cue groans from<i> everyone</i>, as well as laughter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T18:22:47-07:00","id":979384,"title":"","content":"Playing a Hunter game, and the group was in the prologue but had drifted off course. Long story short they ended up in the mansion of a slasher. It was dubbed, &quot;Murder Manor,&quot; or, &quot;Charles Mansion.&quot; The crazed slasher would trap people in his mansion with all of its traps and eventually would kill and eat them. A new player to RPGs yells out, &quot;A MAN EATING MAN IS GONNA EAT MY DAVE ROAST!&quot; (his name is Dave) It ended up becoming the name of the chapter (we have each character record the chapter/game session from their perspective to actually write the Chronicle as a journal/novel)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12209-adonus","name":"adonus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T11:18:02-07:00","id":980347,"title":"","content":"Game is set in a small town, the character (Kurt Crawford) got into a car crash after falling asleep at the wheel (rolled <i>two</i> botches - this is easily my unluckiest character ever). He woke up in the hospital to his mother and big sister, thankfully. Kurt got into a battle of barbs with his big sister, which necessitated a roll (unfortunately, Kurt botched this roll, as well).<br /> <br /> This is a transcript of the game, which you can actually read fully <a href=\"https://witikofalls.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log/case-file-archives\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cKurt\u2026 my baby\u2026 my son\u2026 you\u2019re\u2026 awake!\u201dArlene Crawford rushes into the room. Her sleep-deprived and teary eyes are framed by her creased, worn-out, stress-ridden face. Her reddish-blonde hair has the look of someone who just woke up from sleeping, and not sleeping, on a hospital chair. She\u2019s dressed in jeans, her beat-up tennis shoes, but she\u2019s wearing a faded sweatshirt with Cinderella on it, an old souvenir purchased during one of the Crawford\u2019s vacations to Disney World\u2014back in the halcyon days long passed. She throws her arms around him. \u201cKurt\u2026 it\u2019s me\u2026 I\u2019m here\u2026\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Kurt sighs out of relief; he missed his mother far too much. He accepts the hug, but looks up at his mother\u2019s worn, tired face with a put-on bewildered expression. \u201cWho are you?\u201d he asks his mother. He then cracks a smile after a few seconds, which quickly turns into a cheesy, big grin. </span></span></span><i>I am the master of pranks.</i><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> For the briefest of moments, all color and light drain from his mother\u2019s face. But then, after he cracks his familial sardonic grin, she all but smacks him, then hugs him tightly. \u201cKurt! Don\u2019t\u2026 you\u2026\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Kurt guffaws. \u201cSorry ma! I couldn\u2019t help it! You\u2019re just so serious!\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> But she can\u2019t finish, she\u2019s simply too happy to have him back\u2014her son. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cAbout time you woke up, lazy bones,\u201d comes a voice from the hall. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Kurt hugs his mother back, because he felt the same way\u2014-he had his mother back. The memory of his mother\u2019s foaming, bleeding form causes Kurt to squeeze her tighter.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Kurt then turns toward the voice.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Kurt\u2019s sister Amy is standing in the doorway, dressed in jeans and a black hoodie with a logo that says </span></span></span><i>Cthulhu Loves Pie</i><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. She glares at Kurt like only a red-headed sister can, then bursts into laughter and runs to him, hugging him almost as tightly as their mom. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Arlene strokes Kurt\u2019s hair with her calloused fingers. \u201cWe were so worried. The doctors weren\u2019t sure\u2026 if\u2026 when\u2026\u201d She chokes up. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Amy lays a comforting hand on her mother\u2019s back. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cI won\u2019t lie. I feel like crap. But, honestly, it\u2019s just a broken foot and a really sore head.\u201d Kurt adds, \u201cI was pretty lucky. How\u2019s the car?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> With Arlene still recollecting herself, it\u2019s Amy that answers: \u201cRemember what Demogorgon did to your wizard back in the Temple of Ook-Oz? It\u2019s like that, but worse.\u201d She leans in and whispers only half-sarcastically: \u201cWere you drinking?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cAmy!\u201d Arlene says, snapping back at her eldest with a half-wounded, half-scolding tone.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Amy raises her hands, palms up, as if that\u2019s the most reasonable explanation for all this mess.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Arlene touches her son\u2019s cheek. \u201cDon\u2019t worry about the car, baby. You\u2019re awake, and that\u2019s all that matters.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Kurt chuckles and shakes his head at the half-accusation. \u201cI never drink, Amy,\u201d he replies with a cheeky smile creeping on his face. \u201cI am the good child, remember?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cLying bastard is more like it,\u201d she says, sticking out her tongue. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Kurt laughs some more.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cThat\u2019s enough,\u201d Arlene says, though not without a smile at seeing the good-natured banter between her children. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Kurt looks to his mother and gasps in mock-shock. \u201cFiiiine.\u201d Kurt looks for something to eat; his stomach growls a little. \u201cHave they delivered more food for me?\u201d he asks.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cMy growing boy,\u201d Arlene says with simple maternal pride. \u201cI\u2019ll see if they can bring you an early lunch, or otherwise I\u2019ll go to the vending machine.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cThanks ma.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> She hugs and kisses him as if her love alone will make sure he stays awake and recovers. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">As she leaves, Amy, sitting on Kurt\u2019s bed with her bony hip half-digging into his, leans in. \u201cSo were you? Drinking that is?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Kurt snorts. \u201cWhat? No way! It was still dark when I got up to go pick up ma from work.\u201d He scrunches his nose a little and admits with a touch of embarrassment, \u201cDon\u2019t tell ma this, but I fell asleep at the wheel.\u201d He adds, \u201cI don\u2019t want her to worry about me working too much, y\u2019know.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Amy regards him for a while. \u201cYou had us so freaked, Kurt.\u201d She starts to tear up, then wipes her face. \u201cFuck that.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cYou look so weird when you cry.\u201d Kurt smiles innocently like only a pest of a little brother can do.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cYeah, well you look like shit.\u201d She forces herself to laugh.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Kurt laughs at that.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cYou really do,\u201d she says. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cDo you have a mirror?\u201d he asks, afraid of seeing his own reflection. Afraid of not seeing his own reflection.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cI\u2019m afraid you\u2019d break it. Seriously, you look like Frankenstein had sex with a poodle and the condom broke. An ugly poodle too.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cJesus!\u201d Kurt says. \u201cThanks for the sympathy, big sis!\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cOh, speaking of Jesus,\u201d Amy says, blowing her red hair out of her face. \u201cMom was out of her mind. I mean, she\u2019s been praying and going full on holy roller mode. It\u2019s been\u2026 nuts.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Kurt cringes and groans. \u201cThe last thing we need is Jesus in our lives,\u201d he replies to that revelation.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cYeah, I\u2019m hoping she\u2019ll forget about all those midnight chapel prayers.\u201d She then taps Kurt. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Kurt frowns at that, noticing the plural in \u2018prayers\u2019. \u201cHow long was I out?\u201d he asks.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cScoot over, bum. You\u2019ve been sleeping for two days now in a, well not comfy bed, but a bed. Those waiting room chairs are like the brain-child of a sadistic chiropractor from hell.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Kurt feels a little numb at that explanation, but nevertheless scoots over as directed by his sister. \u201cThat\u2019s longer than I thought,\u201d he replies to Amy. \u201cI told the doctor I thought it was the 8th of October.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> She lays down beside him and sighs, \u201cIt\u2019s the 10th. Friday.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cYay!\u201d Kurt says mockingly. \u201cThe weekend! Woo?\u201d He then adds under his breath, \u201cYou\u2019re so freaking bony!\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cBeats being ugly and short. And gimp.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cHa! You\u2019re short, too!\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cFuck!\u201d Kurt looks at his foot. \u201cThis is totally going to mess with basketball.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Amy closes her eyes. \u201cYeah, it\u2019s going to fuck with everything. Mom\u2019s in denial. I think she had to be. But this is bad, Kurt. I mean, without the car\u2026 and the doctor bills. I tried talking to mom. I think it might work if Rick and I move back in.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Kurt gets quiet as he listens to Amy.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cHelp with rent.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cYeah.\u201d Kurt pauses. He doesn\u2019t like Rick, and the idea of that guy moving back in, that annoys him. But he feels absolutely powerless. \u201cI can talk to my boss Mordecai. Maybe he\u2019ll help out?\u201d he asks. </span></span></span><i>Speaking of,</i><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Kurt thinks to himself, </span></span></span><i>probably should give him a call.</i><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cMaybe,\u201d she says staring up at the ceiling, \u201cBut I thought you said the cinema\u2019s almost belly-up, and has been for years.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cYeah. It is.\u201d Kurt adds, \u201cBut I know he\u2019s got a car that he\u2019s trying to sell.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> She turns on her side, facing him. She rests her chin on his shoulder and puts her arm around him like they used to on the farm\u2019s hammock. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cI could organize a payment plan or something with him,\u201d Kurt offers. \u201cAnd maybe work it off at the cinema.\u201d He hugs Amy back, thankful for the contact after a rough couple days.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cYeah, or you could start pimping Wilson out to the old lonely ladies of St. Enoch\u2019s?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cThey wouldn\u2019t have him. We\u2019ve already tried.\u201d Kurt grins at that.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> She smiles, then sniffs him with mock exaggeration. \u201cYou smell like my cleaning bucket.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cIs that a good thing?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cFor how you usually smell? Yeah, it\u2019s an improvement.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Kurt guffaws. \u201cWhy do I even bother trying to trade barbs?\u201d He then lifts his bum in Amy\u2019s general direction, attempting to fart.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> But unfortunately for both of them, multiple days of a saline diet and left-out egg salad sandwich make for terribly wet, loose stool. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cWha\u2014fuck!?\u201d Amy yells as Kurt soils him and her, given his lack of clothing beneath his back-slit hospital gown. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Kurt\u2019s face whitens. \u201cShit.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> She leaps up and punches him. \u201cYou just shit on me!\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cSorry! I didn\u2019t mean to! I thought it was a fart! I swear I didn\u2019t mean that!\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> She looks down at her brown-smeared jeans. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cFuck!\u201d Kurt swears. \u201cI am so, so sorry, Amy.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cJesus fucking Christ, Kurt!\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cI know Amy! It\u2019s fucking horrible!\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u201cDon\u2019t use the Lord\u2019s name in vain,\u201d comes their mother\u2019s voice around the bend. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Kurt\u2019s face is in his hands and his cheeks are flushed in embarrassment. \u201cGod!\u201d he says. \u201cThe last thing I need is religion! I need a nurse! And a change of sheets!\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Amy stares down as her jeans, agog and gaging. Arlene enters in on the scene. It is an awkward time for all. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kurt:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> But mostly for Kurt.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Mostly.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","user":"Jack","date":". 10-02-2016, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}